WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.613
- [Commentator] Ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.240
it's the tech billionaire death match

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.060
you all haven't been waiting for.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.303
No, seriously, they are planning to fight.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.504
In one corner, Twitter owner Elon Musk!

00:00:16.504 --> 00:00:19.200
(crowd cheers)

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.342
In the other, Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg.

00:00:22.342 --> 00:00:23.553
(crowd cheers)

00:00:23.553 --> 00:00:25.371
(bell ringing)

00:00:25.371 --> 00:00:28.415
(fists thudding)
(fighters groaning)

00:00:28.415 --> 00:00:29.790
(bell ringing)
(crowd groaning)

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.160
- Okay, so yes, this is funny,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.890
but it's also getting kind of serious.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.570
Last week, Elon Musk tweeted

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:39.870
that he'd be up for a cage
fight with Mark Zuckerberg.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.840
Zuckerberg said, "Send me location."

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.630
Musk said, "Vegas Octagon."

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.460
Dana White, the president of the UFC

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.200
told "The Wall Street
Journal" that he has spoken

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.057
to both Zuckerberg and
Musk about a face-off.

00:00:52.057 --> 00:00:54.453
"They are both dead serious," White said.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.350
And now here we are but
this fight is much deeper

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.810
than two big egoed billionaires.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.340
The history of the tech industry

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.830
has been about companies fighting over us,

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.620
the users, and our dollars.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.110
Oh, and yes, different ideologies.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.660
This fight is no different,

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.070
except, well, the possibility

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.380
of a real celebrity death match.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.640
- Let's get it on.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.010
- So, allow me to explain
what's really happening

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.720
in this fight and how it's indicative

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.660
of this new emerging tech battlefield,

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.820
with the help of these guys.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.560
- [Announcer] Custom action
figures may not precisely

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.170
replicate the likeness
of the real individuals.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.450
- [Joanna] Let's look at
the history of this fight.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.510
Musk and Zuckerberg have
actually partnered in the past.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.480
In 2016, Musk's SpaceX
was supposed to take

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:43.268
Facebook's internet
satellites up to orbit until.

00:01:43.268 --> 00:01:45.990
(explosion rumbling)

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:49.290
At the time, Zuckerberg said
he was deeply disappointed.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.290
Things really blew up in 2018 though

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.120
when it was revealed
that Cambridge Analytica

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.630
had acquired and used personal
data from Facebook users.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.400
Musk's Tesla and SpaceX

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.530
deleted their company Facebook pages,

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.350
and Musk tweeted, "It's
not a political statement

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.020
and I didn't do this because
someone dared me to do it.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.610
Just don't like Facebook.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:09.990
Gives me the willies.

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.070
Sorry."

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:14.227
And again, in 2022, he
tweeted something similar.

00:02:14.227 --> 00:02:16.320
"Facebook gives me the willies."

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.700
That was just a few weeks before

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.950
Musk initiated an acquisition of Twitter,

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.270
which officially put these two

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:24.993
up against each other as
competing Social Media CEOs.

00:02:24.993 --> 00:02:27.060
Musk said he wanted Twitter to be-

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.120
- [Musk] An inclusive
arena for free speech.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.110
- [Joanna] He specifically talked

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.550
about political neutrality,

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.380
something he didn't think that was found

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.270
in other social networks.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.220
- My understanding is that

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.870
Zuckerberg spent $400
million in the last election,

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.880
normally in a get out the vote campaign,

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.430
but really fundamentally
in support of Democrats.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.720
Is that accurate or not accurate?

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:49.830
- That is accurate.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.810
- Does that sound unbiased to you?

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.220
- A Meta spokeswoman directed me

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.320
to this Zuckerberg post from 2020,

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.200
which said that these
partisan claims were false.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.610
Meanwhile, Musk has been courting

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:00.810
more folks from the right,

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.880
including Tucker Carlson himself.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.040
So yes, there's differing ideology,

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.130
but also users and money.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.650
In 2022, Twitter reported an estimated

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.520
238 million daily active users.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.710
Meta's Facebook, Instagram, and WhatsApp

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.440
have 3 billion daily active users

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.900
and a far bigger ad business.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.580
But Musk's takeover of Twitter

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.400
has pushed Meta to build
a Twitter competitor,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.560
reported to be called Threads.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.750
It's said to be a
text-based social network,

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:34.080
like Twitter, with
integration with Instagram.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.820
In an internal meeting at Meta,

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.070
a top Zuckerberg lieutenant
said he had heard

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.790
from public figures who
wanted a sanely run platform.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:45.977
That's what actually prompted, well, this.

00:03:45.977 --> 00:03:46.950
(opponent groaning)
(crowd groaning)

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.310
Sure, these guys are very
public about their rivalry,

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:51.660
but it's also representative

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.960
of the broader state of
affairs right now in big tech.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.450
It used to be that
companies were frenemies.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.420
Now they just seem to be enemies.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.860
Just look at this fight chart.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.020
Yes, you have Twitter and Meta.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.400
Then Zuckerberg has been open

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.160
about his beef with Apple CEO Tim Cook.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.260
Apple has limited how much data Facebook

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.440
and other apps can collect
on iPhones and iPads,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.260
and the two now compete
on mixed reality headsets.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.930
Then Google and Microsoft
are now in an AI battle,

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.360
building on its existing cloud fight.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.010
Google has even filed a complaint

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.390
with the Federal Trade Commission

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:28.290
accusing Microsoft of
anti-competitive cloud practices.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:29.760
And then there's Amazon, which competes

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.550
with Microsoft and Google
on cloud services too.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.170
And then you've now got OpenAI,

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:38.010
which Elon also has beef with
and competes with Google.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.470
Yeah, we're gonna need
some more action figures.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.450
So, who is gonna win in this round

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.830
between Zuck and Musk?

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.440
Well, Zuck clearly seems
to have the upper hand

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.910
with his Jujutsu training,

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.897
and a far bigger, more
prospering social media empire.

00:04:51.897 --> 00:04:54.900
But Musk claims to have
a move called The Walrus,

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.020
where he just lies on top of his opponent.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.150
Or hey, maybe these billionaires

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.493
just go in a totally different direction.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.014
Yeah, I doubt it.

00:05:07.014 --> 00:05:09.597
(upbeat music)

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.330
Wanna just go get some Sweet Baby Ray's?

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.163
Sure.

00:05:16.163 --> 00:05:17.370
Wanna come on my private plane?

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.203
We can eat it there.

00:05:18.203 --> 00:05:19.036
Okay.

